  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain showers continue today throughout the \nforecast area. The chance for scattered rain showers accompanies\ncooler temperatures each day through the middle of the week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nEarly this morning, the center of the low pressure system in our\narea continues to drift slowly eastwards along the Downeast\ncoast. This low will continue to gradually shift eastward,\nexiting the forecast area through the day today. While it does\nso, moisture wrapping around the low will continue to support\nongoing scattered showers throughout the forecast area,\nparticularly across the northern half of the CWA as a dry slot\nhas established itself over the Downeast region for this\nmorning.\n\nAs the low pressure continues to pull away into the Canadian\nMaritimes through the early week, the moisture and instability\nsupport will also lessen in our area. That said, an upper level\ntrough will remain overhead through this time, persisting a\ngenerally unsettled pattern with the chance for isolated to\nscattered showers each day. This synoptic pattern will also act\nto support more seasonable temperatures, with highs in the 40s\nto low 50s each day and lows in the 30s through the first half\nof the week.",
